POST /v3/kv/range
{
  "key": "aGlzdA==",
  "revision": "2"
}

examples.response:
HTTP 400 and code 11, `mvcc: required revision has been compacted`

HTTP 400 Bad Request
{
  "code": 11,
  "message": "etcdserver: mvcc: required revision has been compacted"
}

examples.request:
thirty seconds, and ID 0 to mean "pick an id for me"

POST /v3/lease/grant
{
  "ID": "0",
  "TTL": "30"
}

examples.response:
the id the store picked and the TTL it settled on, both as strings

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "ID": "5946617073522799365",
  "TTL": "30",
  "header": {
    "cluster_id": "13155031704180155669",
    "member_id": "2132343088732557958",
    "raft_term": "2",
    "revision": "1"
  }
}

examples.request:
a point read of a key that was written with a lease attached

POST /v3/kv/range
{
  "key": "bGs="
}

examples.response:
the usual kv, plus `lease` naming the lease that owns it

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "count": "1",
  "header": {
    "cluster_id": "12193194121015183211",
    "member_id": "11729749689490407507",
    "raft_term": "2",
    "revision": "2"
  },
  "kvs": [
    {
      "create_revision": "2",
      "key": "bGs=",
      "lease": "4242",
      "mod_revision": "2",
      "value": "YWxpdmU=",
      "version": "1"
    }
  ]
}

examples.request:
the id of a lease that was granted a moment ago

POST /v3/lease/keepalive
{
  "ID": "4343"
}

examples.response:
one chunked line: `{"result": {header, ID, TTL}}`, and the TTL is full again

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "result": {
    "ID": "4343",
    "TTL": "30",
    "header": {
      "cluster_id": "14526714220712277470",
      "member_id": "17966724189823051209",
      "raft_term": "2",
      "revision": "1"
    }
  }
}

examples.request:
an id that was never granted — or was, and has since expired

POST /v3/lease/keepalive
{
  "ID": "999999"
}

examples.response:
the same shape, carrying the id and no TTL at all

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "result": {
    "ID": "999999",
    "header": {
      "cluster_id": "13522108800357880210",
      "member_id": "10296447843658942019",
      "raft_term": "2",
      "revision": "1"
    }
  }
}

